WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.375 --> 00:00:01.584
I thought that was my chair?

00:00:02.043 --> 00:00:03.378
I think this is my better side. 

00:00:14.472 --> 00:00:16.099
All right Ana, what drew you to the film?

00:00:16.766 --> 00:00:18.018
I wanted to work with you again.

00:00:18.018 --> 00:00:18.476
Me.

00:00:18.476 --> 00:00:20.020
Yes, it's true. It's true.

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:22.272
But in a very different capacity.

00:00:22.272 --> 00:00:25.984
Like I knew as soon as I read it
that you and I were going to have a blast.

00:00:26.026 --> 00:00:31.156
Yeah, this is my third collaboration with the lovely de Armas.

00:00:31.239 --> 00:00:33.658
This is actually the first time we get along.

00:00:33.658 --> 00:00:36.161
You know, we've been adversaries for the other films.

00:00:36.202 --> 00:00:38.663
So finally, her and I actually get to work together.

00:00:38.663 --> 00:00:40.081
Like each other a little bit more.

00:00:40.081 --> 00:00:40.415
Yeah.

00:00:40.415 --> 00:00:40.707
Eventually.

00:00:40.749 --> 00:00:42.000
Eventually, we get there.

00:00:45.336 --> 00:00:46.171
Who are you?

00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:47.088
CIA.

00:00:47.088 --> 00:00:48.006
So Sadie, 

00:00:48.006 --> 00:00:52.385
she's this incredible secret agent, and she meets Cole.

00:00:52.385 --> 00:00:54.471
And there's something in Cole that,

00:00:55.388 --> 00:00:56.598
she's never seen before.

00:00:56.598 --> 00:00:59.184
You know, this very weird, clumsy...

00:01:01.478 --> 00:01:02.937
 - Charming, magnetic
- Unfortunate 

00:01:03.855 --> 00:01:06.066
- Irresistible magnetism.
- Clearly.

00:01:06.733 --> 00:01:09.402
Well, I was just wondering if you wanted to, um,

00:01:09.402 --> 00:01:11.237
you know, go out sometime.

00:01:12.072 --> 00:01:12.989
Are you serious?

00:01:15.366 --> 00:01:19.037
I get what your saying though, there's 
something refreshingly honest about Cole,

00:01:19.037 --> 00:01:21.164
you know, albeit a little clumsy.

00:01:24.125 --> 00:01:25.418
I swallowed a rock!

00:01:25.418 --> 00:01:26.711
But they have this really nice meeting.

00:01:26.711 --> 00:01:27.921
They have this great date.

00:01:28.630 --> 00:01:30.757
And then Sadie ghosts him.

00:01:31.174 --> 00:01:33.009
And I don't think Cole deserved it.

00:01:33.009 --> 00:01:35.678
I mean, he was obviously a little too enthusiastic.

00:01:35.678 --> 00:01:37.931
- He kind of couldn't read the room
- Just a little.

00:01:37.931 --> 00:01:39.724
I bet she hasn't even seen your texts.

00:01:39.724 --> 00:01:41.017
Yeah, yeah.

00:01:41.017 --> 00:01:42.310
Go to her.

00:01:42.310 --> 00:01:43.311
I'm going to London.

00:01:43.311 --> 00:01:44.479
Just a little.

00:01:44.521 --> 00:01:46.940
But, you know, she obviously had bigger fish to fry.

00:01:46.981 --> 00:01:47.857
She had a lot going on.

00:01:47.857 --> 00:01:48.691
I was working.

00:01:53.196 --> 00:01:57.033
There really are so many great action
set pieces, whether it's the bus,

00:01:57.033 --> 00:01:59.327
or the plane, or the rotating restaurant.

00:01:59.327 --> 00:02:00.161
Are you ready? 

00:02:00.453 --> 00:02:00.995
Ready for what? 

00:02:00.995 --> 00:02:02.205
No! I’m not!
I’m definitely not!

00:02:06.584 --> 00:02:07.877
That scene in the restaurant,

00:02:07.877 --> 00:02:10.922
was really a challenge
because it was a really big space.

00:02:10.964 --> 00:02:14.843
Yeah, that was one of the few scenes
that we really got to have with Adrien.

00:02:15.218 --> 00:02:18.680
What a romantic spot for our first official date.

00:02:19.430 --> 00:02:22.392
Adrien is such a great energy on set.

00:02:22.392 --> 00:02:24.561
He's so good and so funny.

00:02:24.602 --> 00:02:27.313
I met Adrien in a very different movie.

00:02:27.355 --> 00:02:30.191
And all of a sudden I see Adrien with this mustache,

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:32.694
and french accent.

00:02:34.070 --> 00:02:35.530
What do you go for? Huh? 

00:02:35.613 --> 00:02:37.115
A fairy tale?

00:02:37.115 --> 00:02:38.908
Fairly tales are for children!

00:02:39.951 --> 00:02:40.326
Cut!

00:02:42.036 --> 00:02:43.705
It was really really challenging.

00:02:43.705 --> 00:02:44.914
I think probably the most difficult scene.

00:02:46.207 --> 00:02:48.960
- And of course, I was like in this dress
- You were in high heels 

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:50.628
- and the dress. the hair...woosh.
- And the heels, and...

00:02:50.628 --> 00:02:51.254
Yeah.

00:02:51.254 --> 00:02:51.754
Yeah.

00:02:55.049 --> 00:02:58.303
And the difficulty of, you know, once

00:02:58.303 --> 00:03:02.473
this thing gets out of control and 
starts spinning faster and faster.

00:03:02.473 --> 00:03:03.683
Acting velocity.

00:03:03.683 --> 00:03:04.184
Acting velocity.

00:03:04.184 --> 00:03:04.726
Acting. the...

00:03:04.726 --> 00:03:08.855
the gravity, and the pressure, it was just really really hard.

00:03:09.439 --> 00:03:10.899
You look amazing in that dress.

00:03:12.567 --> 00:03:14.944
And you should wear more suits.

00:03:15.445 --> 00:03:18.698
I really do think this is something
that is going to be for everyone,

00:03:18.907 --> 00:03:19.991
you know, because it does

00:03:19.991 --> 00:03:23.953
have this marriage of comedy and 
action and romance and drama.

00:03:23.995 --> 00:03:26.956
I mean, it checks all those boxes
and it's one of those movies

00:03:26.956 --> 00:03:30.376
that I grew up on that I love dearly
that, that I just don't see enough.

00:03:30.418 --> 00:03:33.296
I feel like it is relevant in today's world.

00:03:33.296 --> 00:03:35.882
And honestly, how do people meet each other?

00:03:36.883 --> 00:03:38.218
Don’t ask me!

00:03:38.218 --> 00:03:39.761
I can barely use my phone.

00:03:41.054 --> 00:03:43.723
And I'm pretty sure there's a lot of texting involved.

00:03:43.806 --> 00:03:44.432
Truely, yeah.

00:03:44.432 --> 00:03:45.725
There a lot of emojis.

00:03:45.725 --> 00:03:46.893
Emoji stuff doesn't count.

00:03:46.893 --> 00:03:47.894
Yes, it does.

00:03:48.978 --> 00:03:50.480
Emoji stuff counts.

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:53.316
Hopefully for everyone out there
who's been ghosted it will give them

00:03:53.316 --> 00:03:56.861
the belief that maybe they were ghosted
because the person was a super spy.

00:03:57.362 --> 00:03:58.613
I have never been ghosted.

00:03:58.613 --> 00:03:59.405
Really?

00:03:59.405 --> 00:04:00.281
It's not true.

00:04:01.241 --> 00:04:04.869
I mean, I admire your confidence, especially
if she's the one who ghosted ya.

00:04:04.994 --> 00:04:06.037
No, no, she didn't ghost me.

00:04:06.037 --> 00:04:08.081
She just doesn't have an international calling plan.

00:04:08.206 --> 00:04:10.291
Oh, right.

00:04:10.291 --> 00:04:14.003
An international art curator
doesn't have an overseas calling plan.

00:04:14.003 --> 00:04:15.171
That's very unusual.

